Where the code comes from

stuffit.py reads StuffIt archives. Its method 13 decompressor was written for this tool,
following compcol 0.8.0 (https://github.com/KarpelesLab/compcol, src/sit13), MIT licensed,
Copyright (c) 2026 Karpeles Lab Inc. Its fixed Huffman tables are copied from there. The
MIT notice for those parts is in stuffit.py and in compcol-LICENSE beside it.

compcol's tables may in turn have come from The Unarchiver (XADMaster), which is under the
LGPL 2.1 or later, so this folder uses the same license.

tome.py reads Apple Installer tomes and their InstaCompOne compression. Its code tables
come from macresources 1.2 (MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2018-2020 Maxim Poliakovski and
Elliot Nunn), the package the script installs, whose instacomp.py decodes the same
compression; tome.py imports them from there. The rest of the format was worked out for this
tool from Apple's MacTCP 2.0.6.

make_system_disk.py, tome.py, and the rest of stuffit.py were written for this tool.
